60: \nL161: 【144†PRINT:†data.bls.gov】\nL162: \nL163: 【145†CPI】\nL164: \nL165: Consumer Price Index\nL166: \nL167:   * 【33†CPI Homepage】\nL168:   * 【146†CPI Overview】\nL169:   * 【147†CPI FAQs】\nL170:   * 【148†Contact CPI】\nL171: \nL172: [Button: Close]\nL173: # Consumer Price Index Summary\nL174: \nL175:     Transmission of material in this release is embargoed until\nL176:     8:30 a.m. (ET) Tuesday, November 10, 2026      USDL-26-1685\nL177: \nL178:     Technical information: (202) 691-7000  *  cpi_info@bls.gov  *  www.bls.gov/cpi\nL179:     Media contact:         (202) 691-5902  *  PressOffice@bls.gov\nL180: \nL181:     CONSUMER PRICE INDEX - OCTOBER 2026\nL182:     The Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U) increased 0.4 percent on a seasonally adjusted basis in October\nL183:     after rising 0.6 percent in September, the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics reported today.\nL184: \nL185:     The index for shelter rose 0.3 percent in October, accounting for over thirty percent of the monthly all items increase.\nL186:     The food index increased 0.5 percent in October, as the food at home index rose 0.4 percent and the food away from home\nL187:     index increased 0.5 percent. The index for energy increased 0.7 percent over the month following a 5.2-percent increase\nL188:     in September.\nL189: \nL190:     The index for all items less food and energy rose 0.3 percent in October, as it did in September and August. Indexes that\nL191:     increased over the month include recreation, medical care, motor vehicle insurance, household furnishings and operations,\nL192:     and education. Conversely, the index for used cars and trucks and the index for communication were among the small number\nL193:     of major indexes that decreased in October.\nL194: \nL195:     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nL196:     \t\t\t\t\t\tOctober 2026 12-Month Percent Changes\nL197: \nL198:     BLS did not collect survey data for October 2025 because of a lapse in appropriations. For most CPI series,\nL199:     BLS could not publish October 2025 indexes. As a result, BLS cannot publish 12-month percent changes for\nL200:     October 2026 for indexes where October 2025 data are unavailable. Information about handling missing data is\nL201:     available online at www.bls.gov/cpi/factsheets/approximating-missing-data.htm\nL202:     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nL203: Table A. Percent changes in CPI for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U): U.S. city average\nL204:  | Seasonally adjusted changes from preceding month  | Un-\nL205: adjusted\nL206: 12-mos.\nL207: ended\nL208: Oct. 2026\nL209: --- | --- | ---\nL210: Apr.\nL211: 2026  | May\nL212: 2026  | Jun.\nL213: 2026  | Jul.\nL214: 2026  | Aug.\nL215: 2026  | Sep.\nL216: 2026  | Oct.\nL217: 2026\nL218: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL219: All items  | 0.6  | 0.5  | -0.4  | 0.1  | 0.4  | 0.6  | 0.4  | -\nL220: Food  | 0.5  | 0.2  | 0.2  | 0.1  | 0.1  | 0.0  | 0.5  | -\nL221: Food at home  | 0.7  | 0.1  | 0.2  | -0.1  | 0.0  | -0.1  | 0.4  | -\nL222: Food away from home(【149†1】)  | 0.2  | 0.3  | 0.2  | 0.3  | 0.3  | 0.2  | 0.5  | -\nL223: Energy  | 3.8  | 3.9  | -5.7  | -1.5  | 2.1  | 5.2  | 0.7  | -\nL224: Energy commodities  | 5.6  | 6.7  | -9.5  | -2.9  | 4.2  | 9.3  | 0.8  | -\nL225: Gasoline (all types)  | 5.4  | 7.0  | -9.7  | -2.9  | 3.9  | 9.1  | 1.0  | 37.4\nL226: Fuel oil  | 5.8  | 3.8  | -9.2  | -1.7  | 10.1  | 15.3  | 2.0  | -\nL227: Energy services  | 1.6  | 0.4  | -0.7  | 0.3  | -0.4  | 0.1  | 0.6  | -\nL228: Electricity  | 2.1  | 0.6  | -1.0  | 0.1  | -0.2  | 0.2  | 0.9  | -\nL229: Utility (piped) gas service  | -0.1  | -0.5  | 0.5  | 0.7  | -1.1  | -0.3  | -0.8  | -\nL230: All items less food and energy  | 0.4  | 0.2  | 0.0  | 0.2  | 0.3  | 0.3  | 0.3  | -\nL231: Commodities less food and energy commodities  